{
  "case": "due2-concept-purpose-prohibition",
  "source": "due2-native (pins decisions/0015 #3-#5: a prohibition on marketing over a SKOS concept scheme written top-down; issues #52, #69)",
  "classification": "odrl-core",
  "needs": [],
  "notes": "Authored for due2; no origin result. The scheme is DPV 2.1's, abridged, and written with skos:narrower, skos:hasTopConcept, and skos:topConceptOf instead of DPV's skos:broader and skos:inScheme. due2 reads the first as the inverse skos:broader edge and the other two as membership (due2-profiles.md §6), so the hierarchy is the one due2-concept-purpose writes bottom-up. dpv:Marketing is in the scheme as a top concept and dpv:DirectMarketing by skos:inScheme.",
